this is a program in quantum information  science which is one of the most  exciting growth areas of science ranging  all the way from physics and engineering  to mathematics and computer science and  we've learned already in quantum  information is that our ideas about what  information is and how one might process  it for communications or for computation  we're in fact too naive the physical  theory of quantum mechanics teaches us  that information has some aspects that  until the past 15 or 20 years no one  really appreciated ever since then we've  been trying to figure out how can we  bring these new insights to bear to  develop completely new paradigms in  computation as well as in communications  and figure out what problems those are  going to let us solve more efficiently  than we were able to with any  conceivable classical computer quantum  information science is first and  foremost a proposes a new technology  quantum computers and the general public  has heard about those that's pretty  exciting but what is less known by  everyone is that quantum information  science also proposes a new way to  pursue knowledge in other areas of  science maybe studying black holes will  inform us on how to build a quantum  computer and new methods to build  quantum computers can tell us give us  insights into condensed matter physics  so we've we've built this extremely  broad group of researcher that cover  many aspects of quantum information  science but what a program like ours  needs to do is not just build a computer  and solve the problem that FedEx has  already ordered but rather try to  demonstrate what determines which are  the right problems to use a quantum  computer for there are no quantum  information science department in any  university it's a new field it is by  definition by definition  interdisciplinary so it needs a place  like CFR where people that would not  meet otherwise can teach each other and  can learn from each other what's special  about C far is that it affords an  opportunity to bring together a truly  multidisciplinary group  people who understand different aspects  of a problem and their everyday lives  don't necessarily have the opportunity  to interface with the people from all  the different aspects of that problem  [Music]
 

